cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this repository in academic work, please cite the AT2SELD technical report (preferred-citation) and, where relevant, the related publications."
title: "Spatial GP-AT / AT2SELD: from General-Purpose Audio Tagging to Spatially Grounded Sound Event Localization and Detection"
type: software
repository-code: "https://github.com/StefanoGiacomelli/spatial_gpat"
url: "https://github.com/StefanoGiacomelli/spatial_gpat"
authors:
  - family-names: Giacomelli
    given-names: Stefano
    email: stefano.giacomelli@graduate.univaq.it
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0009-0438-1748"
    affiliation: "Department of Information Engineering, Computer Science and Mathematics (DISIM), University of L'Aquila"
abstract: >-
  Research code of AT2SELD, a semantic-to-spatial framework that extends General Purpose Audio Tagging
  (GP-AT) backbones toward Sound Event Localization and Detection (SELD): a pretrained audio-tagging
  backbone (E-PANNs) is used as an acoustic prior and connected, through a cross-stitch bridge, to a
  trainable multichannel spatial processing, temporal modeling and track-wise SED/DOA branch. The
  repository contains the training and evaluation code, the staged architecture-search configurations, the
  standalone SELD baselines, the diagnostics (threshold calibration, DOA oracle, cross-dataset projection,
  metric variants, inference-time probes) and the effective-configuration ledger of all executed runs. It
  supports the AT2SELD technical report. Research activities were mainly funded under the Ministerial
  Decree (DM) 118/2023, Mission 4, Component 1, Investment 4.1 of the National Recovery and Resilience
  Plan (PNRR) – “PNRR Research” – CUP: E11I23000100001.
